{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Implementation note before review: docs/cli-reference.md is a GENERATED artifact (header: 'Generated by scripts/gen_cli_reference.py - do not edit by hand', CI drift gate + tests/unit/test_generated_surface_markers.py). Both new tables (verb no-op inventory; old->new confirmation mapping) will therefore be curated as data in scripts/gen_cli_reference.py and RENDERED into the doc, following the existing INTERCEPT_COMMANDS precedent (curated in the generator, drift-gated against source). file_impact updated to name the generator explicitly. AC2's 'test fails when a verb is added without classification' is served by two independent checks: render() raises when the curated key set != rebar._cli._CONFIRM_SCOPE (so the CI drift gate fails), plus a direct assertion in tests/unit/test_mutation_confirmations.py."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787186612771596001,"uuid":"4e88f286-365b-446c-a1c5-ea37b4554e7e"}